        ":question/id": "cafda1d4-be61-508d-b2cb-099e552b1234",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-139426",
        ":question/problem": "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIn index notation, the highlighted entry of the matrix $P$ above is ${p}_{ij},$ where$\\,$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $i=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         and \n$j=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The entry ${p}_{ij}$ lies at the intersection of the $3$rd row and $2$nd column. Hence, we have $i=3$ and $j=2.$"
      },
